WEBVTT

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:39.810
You can have these.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.100
Ooh, thanks.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.920
Sou-kun, were you up late with your telescope again?

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.020
Well, something like that.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.600
You know, this morning, I had a dream about you when you were little.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.820
You were crying, saying, "How can I catch a star?!"

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.370
H-Hey, would you cut it out?

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.640
You were so cute back then.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.400
There's nothing cute about that.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.330
You used to cry about how you wanted a star.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.710
What'd I ever do to you guys? Sheesh.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.230
Here you go, Sou-kun.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.460
Ah, thanks.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:13.890
Oh, dear.
Shoot!

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:14.610
Oh, dear.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.760
Don't worry. I'll do it.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.300
It's okay. You just hurry up and finish eating.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.060
Thanks to you, Kaori's growing up to be a dependable young lady.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.790
Just make some more coffee, Mom.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:27.600
Yes, ma'am.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.650
Come on, Sou-kun.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:46.040
So, what did Sasaki-san say?
Is there a guy she likes?

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:46.620
Dunno.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.370
Come on, ask her!

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:50.790
My friend asked me to find out for him!

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:51.920
Ask her yourself.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.700
No, no, Sasaki-san would get the wrong idea if I did that.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.590
You guys are childhood friends, right?

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.220
Yeah, we are.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.280
Which is why if <i>I</i> asked her
something like that,

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.060
I'd have to deal with the
awkwardness of it on a daily basis.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:07.330
But I mean, she's already turned down
three guys this month!

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.520
Doesn't it make you wonder?!

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.370
You know, out of general curiosity.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:14.520
Besides, you live with her.
Doesn't this kind of stuff just sort of come up?

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.030
Nope.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.000
You get to be right there
when she's in the bath and stuff, right?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.740
And we're talking...
Every! Single! Damn! Day!

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.320
Is that classical Japanese
homework due today?

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.880
Yeah, it is.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.100
Crap. Lemme see yours.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.150
I'll trade it for photos of Sasaki-san in the bath.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:30.960
Kaori!

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.420
Whoa! I was kidding!

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.600
It was a j-j-joke!

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.280
Whoa! What the...?
What's wrong, Yoshida?!

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:35.750
Watch it!

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.720
So, hey, Kaori...

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.340
Nope.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:38.670
Huh?

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.830
I haven't said anything yet.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:43.420
I will <i>not</i> show you my homework.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.310
But I gave you those strawberries.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.480
I will <i>not</i> be bought by some strawberries.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.360
I have a feeling I'm gonna get called on today.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.200
So, you know...

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.040
You always say stuff like that.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.520
I'll get you a slice of cake
...from La Mer next time, so...

00:02:58.590 --> 00:02:59.360
Please!

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.620
Strawberry shortcake, okay?

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:06.560
Th...

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.920
Thank you. Please excuse me.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.940
Aw, I caved for cake.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.530
Really? For cake, huh?

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:17.190
What?

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.310
Fine. We'll say it was for cake.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.720
Hey, mind if I take a piece of fried chicken?

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:31.890
Yeah, I do, actually.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.190
C'mon. Between friends?

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.310
Not on your life.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.020
Hey, Sou!

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.780
This is no time to be eating lunch!

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.990
It looks like there's something exciting going on with our club president!

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:43.410
Huh?!

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.040
She might need backup!

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.700
H-Hold on a second, Kenny!

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.830
I'm still eating here!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.000
Never mind that!

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.100
You, too, Kaori-chan! Let's go!

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.460
Wh-What?!

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.790
Hey, don't touch me!

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.130
Get this girl under control!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.090
Honestly!

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.500
I told you to...

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.960
stop it,

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.030
didn't I?!

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.920
Ooh, that went quicker than I thought.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.090
More like, we were too slow to get here.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.060
So it would seem.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.670
Hanamiya-senpai.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.440
Huh? How long have you been here?

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.260
Let's see...

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.530
Since the beginning, I suppose?

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.180
Then you should have stopped her.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:20.940
Why?

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.070
Oh, you're all here.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.370
No crap.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.780
What the hell were you doing?

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.080
What was I doing?

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.290
Hey, you okay?

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.990
Uh, mediation?

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.380
Why is that a question?!

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.130
Well, I mean, it looked like there was
trouble brewing between these people,

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.860
so I wanted to do something about it.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.590
I didn't plan on things going this far.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:48.350
Th-These guys from the Drama Club attacked us first!

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:51.850
You guys are the ones who broke our signboard!

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.560
Do you have some proof of that?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.150
No, but...

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.770
Wh-Who else would do something like that?

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.160
Huh? So it's a baseless accusation?!

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:02.900
The hell was that?!

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.440
I think, in this case,

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.240
it'd be better if you came clean and apologized.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.640
Wh-Why do you say that?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:08.510
Here.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.860
Wha... This...

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:16.870
The hell?

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.480
So you guys <i>did</i> do it!
Wh-Where did you get that ph-photo?

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.710
That's what you get for making fun of our films!
Wh-Where did you get that ph-photo?

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.120
That's what you get for making fun of our films!

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.630
That's not something you need to know, now is it?

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.130
Th-That's true.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.590
All right! That's enough!

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:29.800
Oh!

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.040
Student Council President,

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.350
Vice President...

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:33.910
Yep.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.150
Well, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.100
Uh, hold on a second.
Well, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:36.880
Uh, hold on a second.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.240
While you're here...

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:42.230
You see, I know the Astronomy Club can be
counted on, so I'd like to ask you a favor.

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:42.950
We refuse.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.730
Who died and made you boss?

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:45.650
Uh-huh.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.550
I'll only need you until the school festival.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.070
And he's not even listening.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.950
To put it plainly...

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.290
Man, I called it, didn't I?

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.490
"Maintain order"? What's with that?

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.780
And why the Astronomy Club?

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:01.630
Isn't that the Disciplinary Committee's job?

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.060
He probably wants to fob off the messy scuffles on us.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:06.260
Here you go, Airi-chan.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.280
Oh, thank you.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.970
Don't do anything too dangerous, okay?

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.420
Even the president said to keep things as peaceful as possible.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:14.210
That's just lip service.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.840
He's totally laughing it up, and we all know it.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.100
By asking us to do this,
he's already made sure it won't end quietly.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.560
Airi-chan...

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.440
I know.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.550
I'll be careful.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:28.230
Just leave me out of it.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:29.230
Senpai.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.200
So what <i>was</i> that thing anyway?

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:35.330
You had it checked out at your research lab, right?

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:37.760
I wonder.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.210
There you go again, keeping secrets.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.630
That reminds me, there was that photo of the Film Society too.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.640
How'd you get that?

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.540
I received it from a member of the Hanamiya Society.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:46.210
Here you go, Sou-kun.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:46.920
Oh, thanks.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.800
The Hanamiya Society is your fanclub, right?

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:51.920
Indeed.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:55.470
They're people who work at my beck and call.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.560
Sou-san and Kenny-san,

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.260
I could let you join as honorary members, if you'd like.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:00.590
Oops!

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:03.160
Yes! You owe me three cans of drink!

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:04.070
Oh, jeez.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.240
That aside,

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:06.830
what is the Astronomy Club doing for the school festival this year?

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.790
Kenny-kun, could I get through?

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:08.940
Oh, sorry.
what is the Astronomy Club doing for the school festival this year?

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:08.960
Oh, sorry.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:11.650
I'd like for us to do something memorable.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:14.950
This will be my last high school festival, after all.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.450
The school festival...

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.620
Oh, I wish I could invite Jennifer over to see it.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:20.740
Here we go.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:24.830
My sweetheart! I wanna hold you tight!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.290
Hey, hey, lemme see her picture.

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:29.450
Don't wanna.

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:31.080
I don't care what we do.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:31.970
I'll leave it to you.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:34.790
You're not motivated at all, are you?

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:39.430
Honestly, I have more fun looking at the stars than participating in school events.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.700
What's so appealing about that?

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:42.800
You know, with stars,

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:46.290
even the ones you can see shining
right now might not exist anymore.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:49.840
Think about how you might never see the stars of this moment again.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.070
It's exciting, right?

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.320
I know! Let's all go see the stars sometime.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.230
I'll provide you with a thorough commentary.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.240
If you insist. Not like I have anything better to do.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:03.350
If we need transportation, I can provide it.

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.520
P-Please do.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.210
Hey, Sou-kun.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.710
How about we try building a planetarium?

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.630
We used to make them in grade school, remember?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.340
They were small enough to fit on a desk.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.400
Oh, that brings back memories.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:20.560
I bet we could make something way more amazing now.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.610
Hmm... Set up a big dome
...and project a sky full of stars...

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.620
Sounds like a big job.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.360
I'm sure we can do it if we all chip in.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.360
I wouldn't mind doing that.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.610
Of course I'll help, Sou!

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:35.800
All right!

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.850
We'll make sure Nagisa-senpai goes out in a blaze of glory!

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.080
Hold on. That has kind of a negative ring to it.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.740
Let's see...

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:49.990
For the projector and star chart,
we can use the reference book from home, and...

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:53.260
Hmm, what to do about the size and materials for the dome...

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:58.220
I have no idea what he's talking about, but Sou sure looks happy right now.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:02.220
Kaori-san understands exactly how to please him.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.340
It's amazing how you never get tired of that topic.

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:11.360
I keep telling you. Kaori's just a childhood friend.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:16.200
Airi, what do you think the max size
would be for the dome?

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.400
I'd want to make it as big as possible.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.820
Well...

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:22.660
As long as we're doing this,
how about we go all out?

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.930
Big enough to fill up this classroom!

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.290
Ooh! I'm starting to get psyched up!

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.320
Airi, what kind of budget do we have?

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.980
Do we need to apply with the student council or anything?

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.920
And you were totally unmotivated
until a moment ago.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:39.400
Gross! You just tried to bite my foot, didn't you?!

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:40.520
Shut up!

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:42.370
You should wear sexier panties!

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:43.140
Hey...

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:45.080
What're you looking at?! You...

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.140
You freakin' creepshow!

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.000
I'm going to head on home.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:50.650
Huh?

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.800
You got something to do?

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.880
Uh... Yeah.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.280
I have to go shopping.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.210
Oh, you do?

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:01.370
Yeah. Well, see you tomorrow.

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:08.980
Can't say I approve of you
hurting fine Japanese ladies, Sou.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:09.750
Huh? Me?

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.640
Go after her.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:12.960
You're so dense.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:14.750
Uh...

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.460
Then I'm off.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:31.650
Hey, what're you pouting for?

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.190
I'm not pouting.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:34.620
What the heck?

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:38.590
Hey, wanna go for cake? You know, cake?

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:48.530
That idiot...

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.130
Morning!

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:02.900
Kaori!

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.450
Airi-chan...

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:05.430
Morning.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:07.250
So you're alone today?

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.180
Yeah.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:12.060
Why don't you two try talking for real?

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.180
Yeah...

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:15.110
Say...

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.080
Hmm?

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.900
About Sou-kun, do you...

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.940
Sou's got feelings for you, Kaori. I'm sure of it.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.990
He just can't express them because he's an idiot.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:24.740
Yeah.

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:27.490
You're so <i>cute</i>, Kaori!

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:44.260
Hey, Sou!

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:48.430
A dustup between the Judo Club and the Karate Club.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:49.570
I can't wait to take them on!

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:51.730
Of all things, talk about messy...

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.440
They're the Judo Club in name only. Bunch of punks.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.020
I can feel my race starting to heart!

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.190
Kaori, you should stay in the club room.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.070
It might be dangerous.

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.930
I don't need you to worry about me, Sou-kun!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.360
You better not think you can mess with us.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:09.030
Shaddup, you punk.

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.530
I'll freakin' kill you.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:10.830
You'd better let me go.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.290
Okay, that's as far as this goes.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.670
Huh? The Astronomy Club?

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.330
So? What happened that things ended up this way?

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.360
Huh? Senpai, when'd you get here?

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:20.690
I've been here since the beginning.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:23.920
It seems one of our first-year students
bumped into one of their second-years,

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.020
and so they came to pick a fight with us over it.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.680
This is so dumb I can barely keep from rolling my eyes.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.850
Aren't you guys embarrassed,

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.650
taking advantage of the fact that the Karate Club
can't touch you because they take their club seriously?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.290
Get real!

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:43.760
That Sasaki Kaori there bribed the Karate Club
with food or lunch or whatever!

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:46.740
And you gave them some of your demo time at the school festival? Seriously?

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:47.840
Talk about pitiful!

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:50.120
That was a formal negotiation.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.960
You're the one who bribed them, right?

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:52.580
Hey!

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.080
C'mon, calm down!

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:56.760
I gave them that to thank them!

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:57.710
Uh-oh...

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:58.260
I gave them that to thank them!

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:00.130
Please take back what you said
about it being a bribe!

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:01.050
Shut up!

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.340
Kaori!

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.810
You son-of-a...

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:18.720
Yeah!

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.160
Don't mess with us, you bastard!

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:22.000
You damn brat!

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:22.910
Take that!

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:27.450
I'm glad it wasn't serious.

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:29.200
Don't be so reckless.

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:32.450
Having a strong sense of justice
can be dangerous if you take it too far.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:36.350
I'll be fine by myself, so you can go on home without me.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.130
How long are you gonna keep pouting for?

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:43.110
Leggo!

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.110
Cheer up already.

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:46.460
Stop that!

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:51.250
Kaori?

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:53.600
You're so unfair, Sou-kun.

00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:55.010
Huh?

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:56.720
You just are.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.280
You know, you guys...

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:03.680
No matter how good your grades are or what athletic records you set,

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:05.990
if you keep going on these rampages all the time...

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:07.590
I apologize.

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:09.570
You say that, but...

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.720
are you really sorry?

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:12.980
And you, Osafune.

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.090
Wipe that satisfied smirk off your face.

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:16.950
I don't mean this as a compliment.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.510
Either way, you guys will need a certain degree of—

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:20.660
Please pardon me.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:21.730
What is it, Hanamiya?

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:24.210
I'd like a quick word with you, sir.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:30.680
I feel like I'm seeing something that I shouldn't be.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:31.590
What?

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.220
Oh, they're back.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:38.480
Okay, I'll let you guys off with a warning this time.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:40.290
Just this once, okay?

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.670
What was with that dumb grin on his face?

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:49.510
You can ask, but I doubt you'll
find the answer very interesting.

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:59.270
It's rare to see you eating cafeteria food.

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:00.210
Hey.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.930
Shiori-san overslept big time today,

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:05.000
so I get to buy my own lunch instead of bringing it.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.180
Oh?

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.400
That reminds me: today's the day
we're going to see the stars, right?

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.450
Yeah, that's right. You remembered.

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:13.570
More or less. So, how's Kaori doing?

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:15.600
She's pouting about something as per usual.

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:18.440
Hey, Sou,

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:21.230
make sure you think carefully about Kaori, okay?

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.980
What are you all serious about?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.770
If you don't, I won't be able to move on either.

00:15:26.770 --> 00:15:27.500
Huh?

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:29.860
Hey!

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:40.080
We've got good weather today,
so we should have a nice view of the stars.

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:42.910
You can leave me out of it.

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:44.710
Go have fun with everyone.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:47.460
It won't <i>be</i> "everyone" without you, will it?

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:52.470
Or more like, what <i>I</i> want
is to go see the stars with <i>you</i>.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:54.220
Well, I'm going to the club room.

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:09.750
Look, those four there.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:11.590
That's called the Square of Pegasus,

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:13.520
and it makes up the body
of the Pegasus constellation.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.750
Man, the breeze feels so good.

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.090
It's putting me to sleep.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:18.620
Didn't listen to a word, did you?

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:23.040
It'd be nice if we could make our
planetarium just as amazing as this.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.520
Wouldn't it, Sou-san?

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:27.880
Um, is that your way of telling me to make it so?

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:33.320
Uh... A Nobel Prize! Billionaire!

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.380
Please don't let Jennifer
get taken by some other guy!

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:37.640
Why don't you wish for bigger boobs
while you're at it?

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:42.650
Hey, stop that.

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:43.770
H-Hold on...

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:46.770
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.150
Don't you have any wishes, Sou-san?

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:52.860
If possible, I'd like it if someone came to my rescue right now.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.040
Is that so?

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.190
What about you, Kaori-san?
That's all you have to say?

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:57.110
I don't have anything in particular...

00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:57.690
Whoa! Hey! Stop that!

00:16:57.690 --> 00:16:58.740
As long as things are peaceful...

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:01.220
What's <i>that</i> supposed to mean?

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.660
Don't go wasting a romantic situation like this.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:05.500
Huh?

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:09.360
I'm kind of thirsty.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:11.890
I'd like something warm to drink, too.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:14.010
I think I saw a vending machine on the way here.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:14.750
You're okay with coffee, right?

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:16.010
Huh? What?

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.970
You're okay with tea, right, Kaori-san?

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.680
What? Uh, um, I-I'll come too...

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:20.970
Don't worry about it.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:23.220
We'll be right back.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.350
Sure...

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:26.730
Thanks.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.230
Honestly! Sou-san makes things so hard for the rest of us.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.840
It's about time Sou paid the sniper.

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:35.870
That's "piper."

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:38.950
Airi-san, are <i>you</i> okay with how this worked out?

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:39.600
Huh?

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.890
I-I don't really...

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:44.450
Here.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.980
When you hit a rough patch, have something sweet.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:48.040
Candy...

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:49.570
A piece of candy?

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.460
There, there.

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:55.940
Oh! There goes another shooting star.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:58.820
Please let the school festival be lively and fun.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:01.140
Man...

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:04.970
If only I could just go floating up
and get sucked into the starry sky.

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:07.730
There you go again with your weird ideas.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.980
It's been a long time since I've seen you not pouting.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:18.120
Sorry.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.670
I'm sorry for sulking like a kid.

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:22.490
I'm sorry too.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.100
Though I'm not really sure what for.

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:30.140
Looks like there won't be any more shooting stars.

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:36.540
I'm back.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:37.220
Oh.
I'm back.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:37.720
I'm back.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:38.340
Wait... Huh?

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.380
Going somewhere?

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.520
Yeah.

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:43.490
We're going to see if there are
any leftover materials upstairs.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:44.400
All three of you?

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:45.810
Nope, just me and Kenny.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.140
What about you, Nagisa-senpai?

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:50.270
I'm going to see the student council.

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.860
So, did things go well yesterday?

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:55.910
Huh? Oh...

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:58.070
It looks like she's cheered up, at least.

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:01.410
Tell me all about it later, okay?

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:04.720
I wanna hear what you said to make Kaori so happy.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:05.360
Huh?

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:08.100
I mean, I said I was sorry, but I wasn't sure what for.

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:08.750
Huh?

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:10.520
What? That's it?

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:11.360
Yeah.

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:12.050
What?

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:14.530
And that's why Kaori's in such a good mood?

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:15.440
I guess?

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:17.760
A-Anything else? Any sweet, conversational lines?

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.640
I'm disappointed in you.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.720
So what exactly are you trying to say to me?

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.020
Ouch!

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:31.020
What was that for?

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.640
I'm utterly disappointed in you!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:42.640
Sou-kun.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.330
I'm going to go home.

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:48.420
The club's run out of tea,
and I want to go buy some more.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:50.290
I have to go before the shop closes.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.160
Got it. You be careful, okay?

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:56.670
What's wrong?

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:59.220
I...

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.550
I love you.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:04.550
What?

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:07.060
Not as family or like siblings,

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:10.560
but a different kind of love.

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:11.560
Uh, um...

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:13.540
Th-Thank you.

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:15.240
No, that's not it.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.190
Uh, I mean, wh-what is this all of a sudden?

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:22.720
I don't want to be just childhood friends anymore.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:26.070
That's why I was mad at you.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.870
Because you...

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.830
I want to know how you feel.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.020
I-I also...

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:36.770
care about you.

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:38.460
A lot.

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:39.840
Okay.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:48.600
I find myself wishing all the time...
that I could b-be with you forever... and stuff.

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:50.100
Okay.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:53.150
No more...

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:54.440
I can't...

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:59.060
Sheesh. You're no fair, Sou-kun.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.410
It doesn't have to be now, so...

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:03.600
Make sure you let me know your answer, okay?

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:04.280
Okay.

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:06.040
Then I'll see you later.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:07.380
Okay.

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:12.180
Got it.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:34.960
Ow...

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:16.760
Sounds like a big job.

00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:19.190
I'm sure we can do it if we all chip in.

00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:21.190
I wouldn't mind doing that.

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:23.440
Of course I'll help, Sou!

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:24.790
All right!

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:27.700
We'll make sure Nagisa-senpai goes out in a blaze of glory!

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:30.670
Hold on. That has kind of
a negative ring to it.

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:36.160
Wh-What was that?

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.410
An earthquake?

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:38.220
No...

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:41.170
An earthquake wouldn't
make a sound like that.

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:43.920
Maybe we should go
see what's going on.

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:44.980
I agree.

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:47.250
I'll hold the fort here.

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:49.460
All right, then let's split up
and check things out.

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:51.820
Uh, then I'll go upstairs.

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:55.710
Whoa...

00:22:56.170 --> 00:22:57.980
It's a disaster zone up here.

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:01.220
I wonder who'll be cleaning it all up.

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:06.070
A dummy?

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:14.820
Sou-kun?

00:23:17.490 --> 00:23:19.830
Sou-kun, what's wrong?

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:24.550
Kaori...

00:23:43.430 --> 00:23:44.400
My name...

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:45.040
She's a transfer student?

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:46.220
What do you do here?

00:23:46.220 --> 00:23:46.980
Looks like you got rejected.

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:48.380
There's been a lot of weird rumors lately.

00:23:48.380 --> 00:23:49.320
There's a rumor about a ghost...

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:51.790
Let's catch that Japanese ghost!

00:23:52.170 --> 00:23:56.900
Episode two: "Proving the Existence of Her and the Ghost."
